* JSCJ BAR64-02V PIN diode model for the matrix switch cell.
*
* This is a conservative datasheet-anchored small-signal RF model, not a
* vendor macromodel. The junction capacitance curve passes through the stated
* maxima of 0.55 pF at 1 V and 0.35 pF at 5 V reverse bias. This deliberately
* exceeds the 0.4 pF typical value at 0 V. The forward model reaches the stated
* 2.5 ohm maximum at 10 mA and 100 MHz.
*
* TT=0 keeps the AC linearization from treating PIN carrier lifetime as an
* ordinary diode diffusion capacitance. The model is valid for the switch
* bias points and small-signal AC analysis, not reverse-recovery transients.
.model BAR64_02V D(IS=1e-14 N=0.93 RS=0.1 CJO=0.783p VJ=0.6 M=0.36 TT=0)
